data/hashing/sha2/

These files are unmodified copies of files in the NIST Cryptographic Algorithm
Validation Program archive of SHA-2 test vectors for byte-oriented messages,
https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/shs/shabytetestvectors.zip,
listed on https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-algorithm-validation-program/secure-hashing.
The archive downloaded on 2026-10-23 has SHA-256
929ef80b7b3418aca026643f6f248815913b60e01741a44bba9e118067f4c9b8.  NIST
publications are works of the United States Government.

The copies keep the archive's CRLF line endings.  They are the ShortMsg, LongMsg,
and Monte response files for SHA-224, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512, SHA-512/224,
and SHA-512/256, and Readme.txt.  The SHA-1 files and the intermediate values of
the Monte Carlo tests are omitted.  The Monte Carlo procedure is that of the
SHA Validation System, https://csrc.nist.gov/CSRC/media/Projects/Cryptographic-Algorithm-Validation-Program/documents/shs/SHAVS.pdf.
